# Paths excluded from the reference sweep and the naming audit. The record layer is
# excluded, never reworded.
#
# UPGRADING.md — the template's own record layer. It is the append-only ledger of
# upgrade entries: an entry is written once, published, and thereafter read by adopters
# at revisions we cannot see, so rewriting one changes what a mid-flight adopter is
# checked against. That is the same reason `MEMORY.md` is excluded by construction.
#
# Its entries carry cross-project citations by nature ("Recorded as agentic-host
# call/0046"), naming the register of the project that authored the change. Those
# numbers belong to that project's rooms and resolve nowhere here, and there is
# currently no form for a cross-project register reference that the sweep accepts:
# bare, prefixed, and inside a markdown link all read as a reference into the local
# room (connollydavid/host#19). Excluding the ledger is therefore the record-layer rule
# applied, not a way around the finding; giving those citations an expressible form is
# owed work, tracked in that issue.
UPGRADING.md

